title: mf:duplicate
tags: [[GUI command]] Duplicates
kind: reference
summary: Scan the active repository for byte-identical files, or keep or trash copies by a query (mf duplicate scan / keep / trash)

`mf:duplicate scan` is the GUI half of `mf duplicate scan`: the whole-repository
scan, with the task bar's progress ([[Finding duplicates]]). Its options stay on
the command line. A cancelled scan is an outcome, not an error: what it found is
kept.

`mf:duplicate keep <query|selection>` and `mf:duplicate trash <query|selection>` are
the GUI halves of <<cmd "mf duplicate keep">> and <<cmd "mf duplicate trash">>
([[Deleting duplicate copies]]), over what the [[metarecord-list panel]] shows —
its effective query, finder and simplified query included — or over the checked
metarecords. An empty selection is nothing to do; it never falls back on the query.
The question names every copy, its groups and the space reclaimed, and is always
asked.

|!Over |!Keep |!Trash |
|the list's query |<<key "mf:duplicate keep query" "e q k">> |<<key "mf:duplicate trash query" "e q t">> |
|the checked metarecords |<<key "mf:duplicate keep selection" "e e k">> |<<key "mf:duplicate trash selection" "e e t">> |

The list is where the rule is built and checked before it acts: on a copy in the
[[duplicates panel]], <<key "metarecord-list:folder other" "b g s">> lists its folder
beside, and <<key "mf:duplicate keep query" "e q k">> keeps what that list shows.
